2026-10-30 07:47:56 INFO areno.api.trainers.policy_only.PolicyOnlyTrainer policy_only.py:723 - rollout_completion={"kind": "rollout", "epoch": 0, "step": 20, "prompt_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. How many ceilings will be left to paint after next week?\nSolution:", "decoded_prompt": "<|im_start|>user\nSolve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. How many ceilings will be left to paint after next week?\nSolution:<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n", "completion": "<think>\nOkay, let's see. Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint in total. This week, he paints 12 of them. Then next week, he paints 1/4 of the number he did this week. So I need to figure out how many ceilings he paints next week and then subtract that from 28 to find out how many are left.\n\nFirst, let me make sure I understand the problem correctly. The total is 28 ceilings. This week, 12 are done. The next week, he paints 1/4 of the same 12 ceilings? Wait, does he paint 1/4 of the number he did this week, meaning 1/4 of 12, or 1/4 of the total number of ceilings? Let me check the wording again. It says \"he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week.\" So yes, 1/4 of the number of ceilings he painted this week. So 12 divided by 4. Let me calculate that: 12 divided by 4 is 3. So next week he will paint 3 ceilings.\n\nThen, the problem is asking how many are left to paint after next week. That would be initial total (28) minus the number painted next week (3). So 28 minus 3 equals 25. Therefore, there will be 25 ceilings left to paint. \n\nWait, let me verify again. Maybe I made a mistake with fractions. If next week he paints 1/4 of the number he did this week, then 12 times 1/4 is indeed 3. So 28 minus 3 is 25. Yeah, that seems right. \n\nAlternatively, another way: when he paints 12 ceilings this week, then next week he paints 1/4 of 12, which is 3. So total painted after both weeks is 12 + 3 = 15. Then 28 minus 15 is 13? Wait, hold on, that contradicts my previous answer. Now I'm confused. Wait, why is that happening?\n\nWait, hold on, maybe I misread the problem. Let me check again. The problem says: \"Next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week.\" So that would mean next week's painting is 1/4 of the number he did this week. So if this week he did 12, next week he does 1/4 * 12, which is 3. Therefore, total after next week: 12 + 3 = 15. Therefore, the answer would be 28 - 15 = 13. But earlier, I thought 28 - 3 = 25. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, there's a conflict here. So which is it? Maybe I made a mistake in the first calculation. Let me think again.\n\nFirst total: 28. This week 12. Next week, 1/4 of this week's 12. So next week's is 12*(1/4) = 3. Total after both weeks: 12 + 3 = 15. Therefore, remaining is 28 - 15 = 13. So the answer should be 13. Wait, so where did I go wrong before?\n\nEarlier, I thought next week he paints 3 ceilings, so no, subtracting 3 from 28 gives 25. But if they're asking for the remaining after next week, maybe there was a confusion between per week. Wait, perhaps the problem is that next week's painting is 1/4 of the previous week's. So the previous week's painting number is 12, next week's painting is 12/4=3. So then total after both weeks 12 + 3 = 15. Therefore remaining 28-15=13. So that would be 13.\n\nBut why did I get confused earlier? Maybe a miscalculation of 28-3? Wait, no, if the answer is 13, then why did I think 25? It seems I must have messed up the miscalculation. So maybe there was a mistake in my earlier thinking.\n\nWait, let me check again with numbers. Let me write down:\n\nTotal ceilings: 28.\n\nThis week, he paints 12. So 12 done.\n\nNext week, he paints 1/4 of this week's current number. Which is 1/4 * 12 = 3. So next week paints 3.\n\nTotal done so far: 12 + 3 = 15.\n\nLeftover: 28 - 15 = 13.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 13. So initially I thought 28 - 3 = 25, but actually it's 28 -15 = 13.\n\nWait, so my first answer was wrong because I didn't consider that next week's painting is 1/4 of the previous week's. So the confusion was caused by miscalculating the second week's number. Now I correctly see that it's 1/4 of the previous week's, not the total. Therefore, the answer should be 13.\n\nBut let me make sure again. Let me do the problem step by step.\n\n1. Initial number: 28 ceilings.\n\n2. First week: paint 12. Left is 28 - 12 = 16.\n\n3. Next week: paints 1/4 of 12, which is 12 / 4 = 3. Therefore, remaining after next week is 16 - 3 = 13.\n\nYes, so that's 13. So the answer is 13, which is 28 - (12 + 3) = 28 - 15 = 13. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{13}.\n</think>\n\nMichelangelo's total ceiling painting is 28. This week, he paints 12 of them. Next week, he paints $ \\frac{1}{4} $ of the number of ceilings he painted this week, which is $ \\frac{1}{4} \\times 12 = 3 $. After both weeks, the number of ceilings left to paint is:\n\n$$\n28 - (12 + 3) = 13\n$$\n\n$$\n\\boxed{13}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. How many ceilings will be left to paint after next week?", "answer": "After this week, Michelangelo will have 28-12=<<28-12=16>>16 more ceilings to paint.\nNext week, Michelangelo will paint 12/4=<<12/4=3>>3 ceilings.\nMichelangelo will have 16-3=<<16-3=13>>13 more ceilings to paint.\n#### 13", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. How many ceilings will be left to paint after next week?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["13"], "solution": "13"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 44406, 87910, 702, 220, 17, 23, 55714, 311, 6177, 13, 1096, 2003, 11, 566, 56848, 220, 16, 17, 315, 1105, 13, 9295, 2003, 11, 566, 686, 6177, 220, 16, 14, 19, 279, 1372, 315, 55714, 566, 1521], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1490, 13, 44406, 87910, 702, 220, 17, 23, 55714, 311, 6177, 304, 2790, 13, 1096, 2003, 11, 566, 56848, 220, 16, 17, 315, 1105, 13, 5005, 1790, 2003, 11, 566, 56848, 220, 16, 14, 19, 315, 279, 1372, 566, 1521, 419, 2003, 13, 2055, 358, 1184, 311, 7071, 700, 1246, 1657, 55714, 566, 56848, 1790, 2003, 323, 1221]}
