th days is 25 leaves. Then, of those 25 leaves, 20% are brown and green, so 60% are yellow.\n\nSo, if 20% are brown and green, then the remaining 60% are yellow. So, total leaves = 25. Then yellow leaves would be 60% of 25. Let me calculate that. 25 multiplied by 0.6 equals 15. Therefore, he collects 15 yellow leaves. \n\nWait, but let me check again. The problem says \"The rest are yellow.\" So if 20% are brown and 20% are green, then the rest is 100% - 20% - 20% = 60%. So yes, 60% of the total collected is yellow. So total collected is 12 +13=25. 0.6*25=15. So boxed answer is \\boxed{15}. \n\nBut wait, maybe I need to check if there's something else. For example, does each day's collection include all the leaves, or are the leaves spread over multiple days? The problem says he collects 12 on Thursday and 13 on Friday. So maybe one day is each day... but that's a bit unclear. However, given the way the problem is phrased, it's likely that the total over two days is 25 leaves, so 60% of that is yellow. So 25 * 0.6 = 15. Therefore, answer is 15, so \\boxed{15}.\n</think>\n\nThe problem states Bronson collects 12 leaves on Thursday and 13 leaves on Friday, making a total of 25 leaves. Since 20% are brown and 20% are green, the remaining 60% (which is 0.4 of 25) are yellow. Thus, the number of yellow leaves Bronson collects is $ 25 \\times 0.6 = 15 $.\n\n$$\n\\boxed{15}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Bronson decides to collect Oak Leaves from around his Neighborhood. He collects 12 on Thursday and 13 on Friday. 20% are Brown and 20% are Green. The rest are yellow. How many yellow leaves does he collect?", "answer": "He collects 25 leaves because 12 + 13 = <<12+13=25>>25\n60% of them are yellow because 100 - 20 - 20 = <<100-20-20=60>>60\nHe collects 15 yellow leaves because 25 x .6 = <<25*.6=15>>15\n#### 15", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Bronson decides to collect Oak Leaves from around his Neighborhood. He collects 12 on Thursday and 13 on Friday. 20% are Brown and 20% are Green. The rest are yellow. How many yellow leaves does he collect?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["15"], "solution": "15"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 19820, 930, 27627, 311, 6530, 18283, 77514, 504, 2163, 806, 61512, 13, 1260, 51207, 220, 16, 17, 389, 7794, 323, 220, 16, 18, 389, 6602, 13, 220, 17, 15, 4, 525, 10471, 323, 220, 17, 15, 4], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1430, 311, 7071, 700, 1246, 1657, 13753, 10901, 19820, 930, 51207, 13, 88190, 11, 279, 3491, 2727, 566, 51207, 220, 16, 17, 389, 7794, 323, 220, 16, 18, 389, 6602, 13, 2055, 11, 1156, 11, 358, 1184, 311, 1477, 279, 2790, 1372, 315, 10901, 566, 51207, 916, 1846, 1378, 2849, 13, 5005, 11, 700, 315, 429, 2790, 11]}
