f of them? If there are 4 matches in that round, winning half of them would be 4 divided by 2, which is 2 matches. So, 2 matches in the last round.\n\nTherefore, adding that to the previous total of 12, he would have won 12 + 2 = 14 matches in total.\n\nLet me check again. First two rounds: each with 6 matches, so two rounds times 6 is 12. Then last round: 4 matches, half of that is 2. So 12 + 2 = 14. Yep, that seems right.\n\nSo the answer should be \\boxed{14}.\n</think>\n\nBrendan wins all matches in the first two rounds, each with 6 matches. This gives him $6 + 6 = 12$ matches. In the last round, he wins half of 4 matches, which is $4 \\times \\frac{1}{2} = 2$ matches. The total number of matches he won is $12 + 2 = 14$. \n\n$$\n\\boxed{14}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Brendan has entered a kickboxing competition and wins matches against multiple contestants. He wins all of the matches in the first 2 rounds, each of which had 6 matches, then wins half of the 4 matches in the last round. How many matches did Brendan win throughout the competition?", "answer": "In the first 2 rounds, Brendan wins a total of 2 rounds * 6 matches per round = <<2*6=12>>12 matches.\nIn the last round, Brendan wins half of the matches which is 4 matches / 2 = <<4/2=2>>2 matches.\nThroughout the competition, Brendan has therefore won 12 + 2 = <<12+2=14>>14 matches.\n#### 14", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Brendan has entered a kickboxing competition and wins matches against multiple contestants. He wins all of the matches in the first 2 rounds, each of which had 6 matches, then wins half of the 4 matches in the last round. How many matches did Brendan win throughout the competition?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["14"], "solution": "14"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1