wn:\n\nBreakfast: 15 - 4 = 11 slices\n\nLunch: 11 - 2 = 9 slices\n\nSnack: 9 - 2 = 7 slices\n\nDinner: 7 - 5 = 2 slices\n\nYes, so 2 slices are left. Therefore, the answer should be \\boxed{2}.\n</think>\n\n$$\n\\boxed{2}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Blanch has 15 slices of pizza in the fridge. During breakfast, she eats 4 slices. At lunch, Blanch eats 2 slices, then takes two slices as a snack. Finally, she consumes 5 slices for dinner. How many slices of pizza are left?", "answer": "During breakfast, Blanch has 15 - 4 = <<15-4=11>>11 slices left.\nAt lunch, she still has 11 - 2 = <<11-2=9>>9 slices left.\nAfter the snack, there are still 9 - 2 = <<9-2=7>>7 slices left.\nFinally after dinner, Blanch has 7 - 5 = <<7-5=2>>2 slices left.\n#### 2", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Blanch has 15 slices of pizza in the fridge. During breakfast, she eats 4 slices. At lunch, Blanch eats 2 slices, then takes two slices as a snack. Finally, she consumes 5 slices for dinner. How many slices of pizza are left?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["2"], "solution": "2"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 91429, 702, 220, 16, 20, 34254, 315, 22502, 304, 279, 37581, 13, 11954, 17496, 11, 1340, 49677, 220, 19, 34254, 13, 2411, 15786, 11, 91429, 49677, 220, 17, 34254, 11, 1221, 4990, 1378, 34254, 438, 264, 39359], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 773, 91429, 702, 220, 16, 20, 34254, 315, 22502, 304, 279, 37581, 13, 6771, 752, 1430, 311, 7071, 700, 1246, 1657, 525, 2115, 1283, 678, 1059, 3607, 15293, 382, 5338, 11, 279, 3491, 2727, 1340, 49677, 220, 19, 34254, 2337, 17496, 13, 5005, 11, 518, 15786, 11, 1340, 49677, 2441, 220, 17, 34254, 13, 4636, 15786, 11, 1340, 4990, 1378]}
