ds per day? Let me recheck. The problem says she has 3 coffee pods every morning. So she uses 3 per day. So over 40 days, 3 times 40 is 120. Each box has 30, so 120 divided by 30 is 4 boxes. Each box is 8, so 4*8=32. Yes, so $32. So the answer should be \\boxed{32}.\n</think>\n\nThe total number of coffee pods Sharon will use over 40 days is 3 pods/day × 40 days = 120 pods. Since each box contains 30 pods, she needs 4 boxes (120 / 30) to cover the trip. Each box costs $8, so the total cost is 4 × $8 = $32. \\boxed{32}<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Sharon’s vacation rental has a Keurig coffee machine.  She will be there for 40 days.  She has 3 cups of coffee (3 coffee pods) every morning.  Her coffee pods come 30 pods to a box for $8.00.  How much will she spend on coffee to last her for the entire vacation?", "answer": "She'll be on vacation for 40 days and drinks 3 cups of coffee/pods per day for a total of 40*3 = <<40*3=120>>120 coffee pods\nHer coffee pods come 30 in a box and she needs 120 coffee pods so that’s 120/30 = <<120/30=4>>4 boxes\nEach box costs $8.00 and she needs 4 boxes so that’s 8*4 = $<<8*4=32.00>>32.00\n#### 32", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Sharon’s vacation rental has a Keurig coffee machine.  She will be there for 40 days.  She has 3 cups of coffee (3 coffee pods) every morning.  Her coffee pods come 30 pods to a box for $8.00.  How much will she spend on coffee to last her for the entire vacation?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["32"], "solution": "32"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 51852, 748, 20161, 18645, 702, 264, 6569, 324, 343, 10799, 5662, 13, 220, 2932, 686, 387, 1052, 369, 220, 19, 15, 2849, 13, 220, 2932, 702, 220, 18, 25374, 315, 10799, 320, 18, 10799, 54587, 8, 1449], "response_token